  "yield" : "Serves 4",
  "notes" : "- Marinating in a savory-sweet mixture of duck sauce, water, and salt makes the chicken tenderloins juicy, mildly sweet, and deeply seasoned.\n- The viscous marinade mingles with the breading to create a craggy, batter-like coating.\n- Sugar in the marinade aids browning.\n- Best results can be achieved by marinating overnight.\n- Use a Dutch oven with at least a 6-quart capacity.\n- Serve with dipping sauces.",
